# SonarCloud Code Quality

This project uses **SonarCloud only** — no local or self-hosted SonarQube server.

Project config: [`sonar-project.properties`](../../sonar-project.properties) (`IWill29_bug-triage-langgraph`).

Dashboard: https://sonarcloud.io/project/overview?id=IWill29_bug-triage-langgraph

## When to run

Run SonarCloud analysis **only** at these checkpoints:

- Before opening a PR (after significant code changes on a feature branch)
- When the user explicitly asks for a quality check, quality gate, or issue scan
- After fixing SonarCloud-reported issues (to verify the fix)

Do **not** run analysis after every file edit, save, or small typo fix.

## How to invoke

### Via MCP (preferred in Cursor)

Requires the SonarQube plugin MCP server authenticated against **SonarCloud** (`sonar auth login -o IWill29`). If tools are unavailable, tell the user to run the **sonar-integrate** skill and restart the session.

| Task | Skill / MCP tool |
|------|------------------|
| Analyze a file | `sonar-analyze` → `run_advanced_code_analysis` or `analyze_code_snippet` |
| Quality gate before PR | `sonar-quality-gate` → `get_project_quality_gate_status` |
| List open issues | `sonar-list-issues` (CLI: `sonar list issues -p IWill29_bug-triage-langgraph`) |
| Fix a specific rule | `sonar-fix-issue` |
| Coverage gaps | `sonar-coverage` |
| Duplication | `sonar-duplication` |

Project key: `IWill29_bug-triage-langgraph` (from `sonar-project.properties`).

### Via SonarCloud GitHub App (primary full-project scan on PRs)

Full-repo analysis and **Quality Gate** on pull requests run through the [SonarCloud GitHub App](https://github.com/apps/sonarcloud), not a local GitHub Actions workflow. There is **no** `.github/workflows/sonarqube.yml`. The PR check *SonarCloud Code Analysis* is the source of truth for merge gating.

The **pr-checker** agent uses SonarCloud MCP (`get_project_quality_gate_status`, issue listing) when MCP is authenticated — complementing the App check before merge.

Do **not** configure or scan against a local SonarQube server (`localhost:9000`).

## Setup (one-time)

1. Install the SonarCloud GitHub App and create/link the project at [sonarcloud.io](https://sonarcloud.io) for GitHub repo `IWill29/bug-triage-langgraph`
2. Ensure `sonar.organization` in `sonar-project.properties` matches your SonarCloud org (default: `IWill29`)
3. Optional: `SONAR_TOKEN` only for local `sonar scan` or CLI — not required for PR analysis via the App
4. Authenticate MCP/CLI for SonarCloud: `sonar auth login -o IWill29`
5. Restart Cursor so SonarQube MCP tools load (they target SonarCloud after auth)
